+## 2026-06-09 (GAP-3 Stage-2 v2 — gate passed, selection still random; LINEAGE RETIRED; GAP-4 spec'd — outer-loop, Claude Fable 5)
+
+- [outer-loop] Operator: "run it" (the panel-specified Stage-2 v2). Built `scripts/experiments/arc3_gap3_stage2v2_mine_real_negs.py` (TRM scored on its own TRAINING split via `evaluate()` with empty evaluator list + de-aug join; 35-min GPU dump, conductor paused/restored) + `scripts/experiments/arc3_gap3_stage2v2_transition_ebm.py` (SpatialPairEncoder with stride-1 hi-res trunk; FiLM-conditioned local energy map, E = global MLP + mean + 0.5·max — the 1-bad-cell detector v1 lacked; structured same-shape near-miss curriculum: component recolor/move/delete/swap + 1–3 cell flips; mined negatives joined per (task, input-hash); gate-1 before any selection eval) + 5 asserting unit tests (`tests/python/test_arc3_gap3_stage2v2_ebm.py`, all pass).
+- **Run:** trained 414 s (early stop 7250), best_val 0.4444 / mean-last-10 0.3913 (harder curriculum than v1 by design). **Gate-1 PASSED: synthetic same-shape near-miss AUROC 0.7893** (bar 0.70). **Selection eval STILL ~random:** EBM_TTA pass@2 0.1613 vs random 0.1432 (P(X≥5)=0.468) vs vote 0.4516; real-candidate AUROC 0.46–0.49; union value-add zero. `results/arc3_gap3_stage2v2_transition_ebm.json`.
+- **Adversarial round (`results/arc3_gap3_stage2v2_adversarial_verify.json`): 5/5 NEGATIVE_CONFIRMED; retirement adjudicated TRUE (one dissent refuted on yield/ceiling/signal-class grounds); worst severity major — attached to the artifact's self-description, all numbers reproduced bit-for-bit.** Decisive forensics (now in-place as `corrigendum_2026_06_09_stage2v2`): (1) the mined-real axis was a **silent no-op** — miner de-aug bug (`inv_fn(_crop(...))` empty on translation-augmented rows) keyed 240/250 mined negatives to empty-grid hashes; effective exposure 10 negs / 3 tasks / 0.04% of curriculum; (2) the mining premise is **structurally barren** — "59.9% wrong" was a padding artifact ~500× off; TRM memorizes its train split (genuine error rate 10/8,259 = 0.12%); (3) **gate-1 was a self-licking ice cream cone** — the v1 model passes the identical synthetic gate at 0.7291; synthetic gates measure curriculum-fitting, not transfer; (4) the near-miss curriculum **regressed the dominant class** (same-shape wrong-rule applications, 59.1% of errors): 0.502 macro / 0.3283 pair-weighted, below chance, worse than v1 — it teaches "gold+small defect=bad"; (5) TTA non-replication; (6) independence violation in the helpful direction — and still random.
+- **Disposition:** trained-content-energy selector lineage **RETIRED** per the v1 panel's pre-registered condition — added to `ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml` (`gap3_trained_content_energy_selector_retired_stage2v2_2026_06_09`, operator_reopen_required + gate-1R precondition). Honest bound + the distilled **GAP-4: same-shape rule-application consistency** missing-verifier spec recorded in `ops/verifier_gaps.md` (candidate design: execution/program-synthesis verification — induce the rule as a program, execute, compare; the ARC-AGI-3 M2-v3/v4 codex+consistency-energy stack is the in-house precedent). Miner bugs documented in the script docstring (preserved as evidence; lineage retired, not fixed for reuse).
