ce (early checkpoint / different seed / cross-fold) is a NEW design carrying the exact distribution-shift trap that killed v1. (2) CEILING \u2014 even with a perfect dataset, measured in-distribution mastery is 0.79 AUROC / 0.444 top-1 with ~36% synthetic\u2192real transfer efficiency; the lineage's real-class ceiling across two architectures and two curricula is ~0.63-0.69, while matching vote's pass@2=0.4516 needs per-task AUROC ~0.92-0.99 (the vote-missed headroom tasks need 0.996-0.999: gold with 2 votes among 599 candidates; 1-cell diff among 754; a uniform 0.90 AUROC yields only pass@2\u22480.29; headroom golds rank mid-pack by E: 186/599, 486/754; 4/5 headroom golds Pareto-dominated in (votes,E)). (3) SIGNAL CLASS \u2014 the only above-chance reading reviewer 1 cites (0.6038 on the <=5%-cell class) is the MINOR class (11-12% of wrong-pair mass); the dominant class \u2014 same-shape plausible-but-wrong rule applications, 59.1% of real errors / 81.4% of pairs \u2014 sits at 0.502 macro / 0.3283 pair-weighted, BELOW chance and REGRESSED from v1 (0.6283/0.4707), mechanistically because the near-miss curriculum teaches \"gold+small defect=bad\" while the curriculum's median changed-cell fraction is 0.083 vs the real pool's 0.40. Vote's 0.92-0.98 on that class is generator-marginal signal, not content signal \u2014 it proves the class is discriminable by SOME information source, not by a content energy. Reviewer 1's own caveat concedes \"rule-level discrimination at 1.27M params remains a long shot.\" No quantified path to 0.92 exists; retirement stands.\n\nGATE-1 BLIND SPOT (reviewer 2's decisive contribution): the gate is a self-licking ice cream cone \u2014 the v1 model (\"predictably doomed\") PASSES v2's synthetic gate at 0.7291 against the 0.70 bar, so the gate never discriminated v2 from v1; the artifact's \"v1 measured 0.481 here\" contrast is a category error (v1's REAL-pool near-miss AUROC vs the SYNTHETIC gate), and v2's own real-pool <=5%-cell AUROC is 